    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>That sounds like a solid foundation. One specific area I'm worried about is the \"threat landscape\" during the hand-off points at the airports. We've had issues with local ground handlers being a bit careless with the thermal packaging, or even cases where shipments were tampered with or moved to non-refrigerated zones during delays. \n\nHow should we structure our security and oversight protocols to prevent these kinds of external disruptions or \"unauthorized interference\" from compromising the temperature integrity during those vulnerable transfer windows?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
